</div>', '<div class="toolkit-section">
<div class="toolkit-section-label">Client Profiles to Target</div>
<p>High-priority: DIY investors who made reactive changes during the crisis drawdown and are now reconsidering -- they need a framework for thinking about re-entry, not just a price level. Clients of advisors who went quiet during the crisis and are now calling only to take credit for the rally. Mortgage holders with variable-rate renewals in 2026 who are now incorrectly assuming the rate picture has improved because oil dropped for one day. Medium-priority: Business owners in transportation, manufacturing, and construction who have been managing higher input costs. Retirees in drawdown who made allocation changes during the drawdown and need help thinking through whether to undo them.</p>
</div>
<div class="toolkit-section">
<div class="toolkit-section-label">Opening Line</div>
<div class="script-box">"Hi [Name], I know yesterday''s rally felt like a big exhale after a stressful few weeks. I wanted to reach out because the next two weeks are actually the most important of the whole crisis from a portfolio standpoint -- and I think a lot of people are going to make decisions they''ll regret based on one day of market movement. Do you have 15 minutes? I''d like to walk you through what actually happened and what it means for someone in your situation."</div>
</div>
<div class="toolkit-section">
<div class="toolkit-section-label">Value Proposition</div>
<p>The advisor''s value in a relief rally is harder to articulate than the value in a crisis -- but it''s just as real. Anyone can tell a client the market went up. The advisor who can explain why yesterday''s rally may be premature, what the next two weeks of negotiations mean, and how to think about positioning going into the Bank of Canada''s April 29 decision is providing something qualitatively different from a news headline. That calm, grounded framework -- delivered before the client makes an emotional re-entry decision -- is the difference between a transaction and a relationship.</p>
</div>
<div class="toolkit-section">
<div class="toolkit-section-label">Discovery Questions</div>
<ul>
<li>What did you do with your portfolio when things got rough over the last six weeks?</li>
<li>Are you thinking about making any changes based on yesterday''s rally, or are you holding where you are?</li>
<li>Do you have a variable-rate mortgage renewing this year? Has anyone walked you through what the Bank of Canada''s next decision means for your payment?</li>
<li>When the market dropped during the Iran crisis, did you have someone to call, or were you working through it on your own?</li>
<li>If the ceasefire breaks down in the next two weeks and oil goes back above $100, what does that mean for your portfolio -- and do you have a plan for it?</li>
</ul>
</div>
<div class="toolkit-section">
<div class="toolkit-section-label">Prospecting Email Template</div>
<div class="email-box" id="prospect-email">
<strong>Subject:</strong> Yesterday''s rally -- what it actually means before you make any moves<br><br>
